meta {
  name: Create Bug Report
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/bug-reports
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "description": "The leaderboard still shows last month's numbers after I record a sale.\nSteps: record a sold deal, go back to the dashboard, the Motivation Hub total is unchanged.",
    "severity": "high",
    "screenshots": [
      {
        "key": "{{bugScreenshotKey}}",
        "filename": "leaderboard-stale.png",
        "contentType": "image/png",
        "size": 20480
      }
    ],
    "context": {
      "url": "http://localhost:5173/dashboard/producer?range=month",
      "route": "/dashboard/producer",
      "userAgent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_15_7) Bruno/CLI",
      "viewport": { "width": 1512, "height": 916 },
      "theme": "dark"
    }
  }
}

script:post-response {
  // Read back by `Platform Bug Reports`, which sorts after this folder.
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    bru.setVar("bugReportId", res.getBody().id);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("returns a receipt, not the triage record", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("id");
    expect(body).to.have.property("createdAt");
    // The reporter must not be handed the status or the internal notes.
    expect(body).to.not.have.property("status");
    expect(body).to.not.have.property("internalNotes");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /bug-reports — file a report (step 3 of 3)

  What the floating "Report a bug" widget submits, from any signed-in surface.

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`)
  - **Permission:** **none** — any authenticated caller. See
    `Presign Screenshot` for why.
  - **Data scope:** none (`@SkipTenant()`, `@SkipBranch()`)
  - **Rate limit:** `BUG_REPORT_RATE_LIMIT` (default 10) per minute.

  ## Body
  | field       | type   | rules                                              |
  |-------------|--------|-----------------------------------------------------|
  | description | string | 10–5,000 chars                                      |
  | severity    | enum   | `low` \| `normal` \| `high` \| `blocking` (default `normal`) |
  | screenshots | array  | ≤ 5, each `{ key, filename, contentType, size }`     |
  | context     | object | all fields optional — url, route, userAgent, viewport, theme |

  ## What the server does not take your word for

  - **Identity.** `reportedBy`, `reporterEmail`, `reporterName`, `agencyId` and
    `branchId` come from `request.access` and the user document, never from the
    body. There is no way to file a report as somebody else.
  - **Screenshot ownership.** Every `key` is re-checked against the caller's own
    `agencies/<agencyId>/bug-reports/<userId>/` prefix. A key from anywhere else
    is a `400`.
  - **Screenshot size and type.** Re-read from storage with `HeadObject`. A
    presigned PUT signs only the content type, so the declared `size` is a claim
    about a file the API has never seen.
  - **A key that was presigned but never uploaded to** is **dropped**, and the
    report is still created. Losing one screenshot beats losing the report it was
    attached to.

  `context` is client-supplied and only ever displayed. Nothing authorizes off it.

  ## Response `201`
  ```json
  { "id": "68f3…c21", "createdAt": "2026-09-01T14:22:07.113Z" }
  ```

  A receipt, not the record: the reporter never sees `status` or
  `internalNotes`. Reading a report is `platform:bugs:read`.

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — description under 10 chars, more than 5 screenshots, or
    a screenshot key the caller was not issued.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired token.
  - `429 Too Many Requests` — over the per-minute limit.
}
